# Internal URLs

`InternalUrlsPlugin` lets you register custom `internal://` (or custom-scheme) pages that render inside `<Frame>` and `<Tabs>` without going through Scramjet.

Pages can be Svelte 5 components, snippets, or HTML strings, and integrate automatically with the address bar, autocomplete, tab titles and favicons, back/forward navigation, reload, and `persist`.

## Setup

Create an `InternalUrlsPlugin` instance and pass it to `<Chemical plugins={[...]}>` to enable it across all frames and tabs, or pass it directly to a single `<Frame>` or `<TabFrame>`.

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";
  import { InternalUrlsPlugin } from "chemicaljs/InternalUrlsPlugin";
  import {
    AddressBar,
    Autocomplete,
    NewTab,
    Tab,
    TabBar,
    TabClose,
    TabFavicon,
    TabFrame,
    Tabs,
    TabTitle,
  } from "chemicaljs/tabs";
  import Settings from "./Settings.svelte";
  import History from "./History.svelte";

  let chemical = $state();
  let ready = $state(false);
  let tabs = $state();

  const internalUrls = new InternalUrlsPlugin({
    routes: {
      settings: {
        title: "Settings",
        component: Settings,
      },
      history: {
        title: "History",
        component: History,
      },
      about: {
        title: "About",
        html: "<h1>Chemical</h1><p>Custom internal page</p>",
      },
    },
  });
</script>

<Chemical bind:ready bind:this={chemical} plugins={[internalUrls]}/>

<Tabs bind:this={tabs} persist {chemical} {ready}>
  <TabBar>
    <Tab>
      <TabFavicon>🌐</TabFavicon>
      <TabTitle/>
      <TabClose>✕</TabClose>
    </Tab>
    <NewTab>+</NewTab>
  </TabBar>

  <div>
    <button onclick={() => tabs.back()} disabled={!tabs?.canBack()}>‹</button>
    <button onclick={() => tabs.forward()} disabled={!tabs?.canForward()}>
      ›
    </button>
    <button onclick={() => tabs.reload()}>↻</button>
    <AddressBar placeholder="Search or enter URL"/>
    <Autocomplete/>
    <button onclick={() => tabs.go("internal://settings")}>Settings</button>
  </div>

  <TabFrame/>
</Tabs>
```

### Standalone Frame Usage

```svelte
<script>
  import Chemical from "chemicaljs/Chemical";
  import Frame from "chemicaljs/Frame";
  import { InternalUrlsPlugin } from "chemicaljs/InternalUrlsPlugin";
  import Settings from "./Settings.svelte";

  let chemical = $state();
  let ready = $state(false);
  let frame = $state();

  const internalUrls = new InternalUrlsPlugin({
    routes: {
      settings: { title: "Settings", component: Settings },
    },
  });
</script>

<Chemical bind:ready bind:this={chemical}/>
<Frame bind:chemical bind:ready bind:this={frame} plugins={[internalUrls]} src="internal://settings"/>
```

## Options

```js
new InternalUrlsPlugin({
  scheme: "internal",
  routes: {},
  fallback: undefined,
  history: false,
});
```

| Option | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `scheme` | `string` | `"internal"` | URL scheme prefix (e.g. `"internal"` matches `internal://...`). |
| `routes` | `Record<string, Route>` | `{}` | Map of route patterns to route definitions. |
| `fallback` | `Route` | Built-in 404 page | Rendered when a matching scheme URL does not match any route. |
| `history` | `boolean` | `false` | Whether internal page visits are added to `getHistory()`. Can be overridden per route. |

You can also add or remove routes dynamically with `plugin.register(pattern, route)` and `plugin.unregister(pattern)`.

## Defining Routes

Each route entry can be an object, a Svelte component directly, or an HTML string directly:

```js
new InternalUrlsPlugin({
  routes: {
    settings: SettingsComponent,
    about: "<h1>About</h1>",
    history: {
      title: "History",
      favicon: "data:image/svg+xml,...",
      component: HistoryComponent,
      props: { showSearch: true },
      history: false,
    },
    "docs/:slug": {
      title: ({ params }) => `Docs: ${params.slug}`,
      component: DocsPage,
    },
    "files/*": {
      title: "Files",
      html: ({ params }) => `<h1>Path: ${params["*"]}</h1>`,
    },
    "*": {
      title: "Not Found",
      html: ({ url }) => `<h1>Unknown page: ${url}</h1>`,
    },
  },
});
```

| Route Field | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `component` | `Component` | Svelte 5 component rendered inside the frame viewport. |
| `snippet` | `Snippet` | Svelte 5 snippet rendered with the internal route context. |
| `html` | `string \| (ctx) => string` | HTML document rendered inside an isolated `srcdoc` iframe. |
| `props` | `object \| (ctx) => object` | Extra props merged into `component`. |
| `title` | `string \| (ctx) => string` | Tab/frame title (defaults to the `<title>` tag for HTML routes, or the route path). |
| `favicon` | `string \| (ctx) => string` | Favicon data URL (defaults to `<link rel="icon">` `data:` URI for HTML routes). |
| `history` | `boolean` | Overrides the plugin's default `history` recording setting for this route. |

## Component Props

Svelte components (and snippets, via their argument) automatically receive navigation, history, and URL context:

```svelte
<script>
  let {
    url,
    path,
    params,
    searchParams,
    hash,
    go,
    openTab,
    back,
    forward,
    reload,
    setTitle,
    setFavicon,
    getHistory,
    removeHistory,
    clearHistory,
    chemical,
    tabs,
  } = $props();
</script>

<h1>History</h1>
<button onclick={() => clearHistory()}>Clear all</button>

{#each getHistory() as entry (entry.id)}
  <div>
    <button onclick={() => go(entry.url)}>{entry.title}</button>
    <button onclick={() => removeHistory(entry.id)}>✕</button>
  </div>
{/each}
```

## HTML Page Bridge

HTML routes (`html: ...`) run inside a `srcdoc` iframe with automatic link handling and a `window.chemical` helper:

* `<a href="https://example.com">` and `<a href="internal://settings">` navigate inside the frame.
* `<a href="..." target="_blank">` and `window.open(...)` open a new tab when inside `<Tabs>`.
* `window.chemical` exposes `url`, `scheme`, `path`, `params`, `searchParams`, `hash`, `go`, `back`, `forward`, `canBack`, `canForward`, `reload`, `open`, `setTitle`, and `setFavicon`.

## Autocomplete

When registered on `<Chemical plugins={[internalUrls]}>`, typing `internal://` in `<AddressBar>` suggests matching static routes directly in `<Autocomplete>` without sending queries to Google.